   Euc'lid Avenue leads east away from Central Square.  The houses here
were tall and narrow, built shoulder to shoulder, and now they lean
against one another like weary drunks, threatening to collapse at any
moment.  Dried blood is splashed across their doorsteps.  The square
lies to the west.
