   You have descended into Lancius' basement, a low, cool room with
walls of rough-cut stone.  Shelves line the walls, stacked with jars of
preserves, coils of rope and casks of wine, and a narrow cot has been
pushed into one corner as if someone has been hiding down here.  The air
smells of earth and candle wax.  A door leads back up into the house.
